          "settings": {
            "question": "What are curved barbells?",
            "answer": "<p>Curved barbells are a type of body jewellery shaped with a gentle curve and ball or gem ends on both sides. Also known as <strong>banana bars</strong>, they are designed to follow the natural contours of the body for a comfortable and secure fit.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_Lic6Gn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What piercings can curved barbells be used for?",
            "answer": "<p>Curved barbells are versatile and suitable for a wide range of piercings, including <strong>eyebrow</strong>, <strong>rook</strong>, <strong>daith</strong>, <strong>vertical labret</strong>, <strong>belly button (navel)</strong>, <strong>intimate piercings</strong>, and <strong>some ear cartilage piercings</strong>. The shape reduces pressure and enhances comfort, especially in curved or angled piercings.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_CNiE6e": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean and care for my curved barbell?",
            "answer": "<p>Clean your jewellery with warm water and mild soap, then dry it gently with a soft cloth. Avoid harsh cleaners or alcohol-based solutions. For piercings that are still healing, use sterile saline to keep the area clean and healthy.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_FQUd4a": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What materials are your curved barbells made from?",
            "answer": "<p>We offer curved barbells in <strong>implant-grade titanium</strong>, <strong>solid gold</strong>, <strong>925 sterling silver</strong>,<br/>and <strong>316L surgical steel</strong>. All are made to professional standards, with smooth, polished finishes for comfort and durability. Titanium and gold are recommended for sensitive skin or healing piercings.</p>",
